Hosted on **AWS Amplify** (AWS profile `customapp`, region **eu-west-1**), app `<APP_NAME>`, app id `<APP_ID>`, connected to GitHub repo `<ORG/REPO>`. Each git branch with auto-build deploys on push.

## Test-user URLs

<!-- Multi-tenant portals: append the tenant param, e.g. ?bg=<tenant-guid> -->

| Env | URL | Git branch |
|-----|-----|-----------|
| dev | `https://<DEV_HOST>/` | `dev` |
| demo | `https://<DEMO_HOST>/` | `demo` |

- Prefer the custom-domain URLs over the raw `*.<APP_ID>.amplifyapp.com` Amplify URLs.
- Static files are served from the repo root and are **case-sensitive**.

## Notes

- Promotion flow: `dev` -> `demo` -> `uat` -> `prod` (uat/prod may not be wired in Amplify).
- When adding a new subdomain/environment, add `<env>-<slug>.<domain>` to the allowed OAuth redirect/callback URLs (Azure/Google) and Supabase allowed URLs, or logins will fail.
- Hosting is wired at the AWS-account level via the Amplify GitHub App - there is no hosting config file in the repo (no netlify/vercel/workflows). Do not conclude "no deployment exists" from a repo search.
